  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/he-p1600.html",
  "prefLabel": "He-P 1611.04 Examinations, Assessments, and Course Completion Certificates",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "He-P 1611.04 Examinations, Assessments, and Course Completion Certificates.\n\n(a) At the conclusion of each program, each student shall complete an examination and if applicable, a hands-on skills assessment, or in the alternative, a proficiency test that tests the student’s knowledge of all required content areas.\n\n(b) Each student completing an examination as required by (a) above shall receive a passing score of 70% or greater to pass any course, or successfully complete a proficiency test developed and assessed according to the program manager’s criteria.\n\n(c) Hands-on skills assessments in (a) above shall:\n\n(1) Incorporate actual field conditions and current work practices;\n\n(2) Evaluate the ability of the student to correctly perform all work practices and procedures that were covered in the hands-on skills portion of the course; and\n\n(3) Be graded on a pass/fail basis and in accordance with the hands-on skills assessment developed by the program manager.\n\n(d) Each student who successfully completes the course, including class attendance and passage of the examination, and if applicable, a hands-on skills assessment or a proficiency test shall receive a course completion certificate.\n\n(e) The certificate shall include:\n\n(1) The name, address, telephone number, and certification number of the provider of the program;\n\n(2) The discipline of lead professional for which the completed educational program is certified;\n\n(3) If it was taught electronically or in-person;\n\n(4) The language in which the course was taught, if other than English;\n\n(5) The number of course hours in person versus e-learning;\n\n(6) The dates of the course;\n\n(7) The name of the student; and\n\n(8) A unique certificate number.\n\n(f) Course completion certificates shall be valid for one year.\n\nSource. #5920, eff 1-1-95; amd by #6096, eff 9-22-95; ss by #7181, eff 12-24-99; amd by #7393, INTERIM, eff 10-28-00, EXPIRED: 4-26-01; ss by #7495, eff 5-23-01; ss by #8039, eff 2-13-04; ss by #8932, eff 7-6-07; ss by #9986, eff 9-1-11, EXPIRED: 9-1-11\n\nNew. #13052, eff 6-11-20; ss by #14230, eff 4-2-25; ss by #14680, eff 8-26-26, EXPIRES: 8-26-36",
